### Rashmatz Server — Interactive HTTP Test File
### Works in Visual Studio, VS Code (REST Client), and JetBrains Rider.
### Start the server first: dotnet run --project src/Rashmatz.Server.fsproj

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@adminEmail = admin@rashmatz.org
@memberEmail = soldier@rashmatz.org

# Deterministic Dev Seed IDs (created automatically in Development mode)
@warehouseId = 44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444443
@memberId = 44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444442
@templateId = 99999999-9999-4999-8999-999999999991
@radio1Id = 77777777-7777-4777-8777-777777777771
@batteryTypeId = 66666666-6666-4666-8666-666666666662

### 1. OpenAPI Specification (used by Swagger / Scalar / Schemathesis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### 2. Ensure Dev Database Seed (idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/seed

### 3. Page 1 — Login Bootstrap (unauthenticated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/login?return_to=/my-custody

### 4. Dev Login as Soldier (issues 30-day HttpOnly session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}"
}

### 5. Page 2 — My Custody (using X-Dev-User-Email header, no UI needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/my-custody
# X-Dev-User-Email: {{memberEmail}}

### 6. Page 2 — My Custody with X-Holders-Hash (replace hash from step 5 to get holders_directory: null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/my-custody
# X-Dev-User-Email: {{memberEmail}}
# X-Holders-Hash: fe8cd2dac2654142

### 7. Page 5 — Quick Relocation Bootstrap (last 20 relocated items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/items-relocate
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}

### 8. Page 5 — Search Serialized Items using HTTP QUERY method
QUERY {{baseUrl}}/serialized-items/lookup
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "q": "PRC"
}

### 8b. Page 5 — Search Serialized Items using HTTP QUERY method
POST {{baseUrl}}/serialized-items/lookup
# X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Http-Method-Override: QUERY

{
  "q": "PRC"
}


### 9. Page 5 — Relocate Serialized Item (Physical Location only, no custody change)
POST {{baseUrl}}/serialized-items/{{radio1Id}}/relocate
# X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to_location_holder_id": "{{warehouseId}}",
  "to_location_custom_text": "Shelf B2, Bin 4",
  "notes": "Moved after battery check"
}

### 10. Page 6A — Transfer Step 1: Choose Template
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/transfers-new-template
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}

### 11. Page 6B — Transfer Step 2: Select Parties (pre-populated from template)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/transfers-new-parties?template_id={{templateId}}
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}

### 12. Page 6C — Transfer Step 3: Load Source Inventory, Dest Balances & Template Lines
GET {{baseUrl}}/pages/transfers-new-items?source_id={{warehouseId}}&dest_id={{memberId}}&template_id={{templateId}}
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}

### 13. Page 6C — Check Unassigned Barcode (HTTP QUERY)
QUERY {{baseUrl}}/serialized-items/check-unassigned
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "barcode": "BC-NEW-999"
}

### 14. Page 6C — Commit Custody Transfer (with Idempotency-Key & Physical Location Sync)
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
X-Dev-User-Email: {{adminEmail}}
Idempotency-Key: 10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "source_holder_id": "{{warehouseId}}",
  "dest_holder_id": "{{memberId}}",
  "transfer_template_id": "{{templateId}}",
  "serialized_item_ids": ["{{radio1Id}}"],
  "quantitative_lines": [
    { "item_type_id": "{{batteryTypeId}}", "quantity": 4 }
  ],
  "update_physical_location": true,
  "to_location_custom_text": "Field Vest Pouch 2",
  "notes": "Issued standard comms kit"
}
